// #3637: the prelude's `ord_max` stays refused at `Double`, with the
// concrete-type edit named. `Ord` reaches no witness (`<` on an erased `T` is
// the raw comparison), so a `Double` would be ordered by its box, not its
// value. `cmp_eq` is the one prelude helper whose bound reaches a witness,
// and it answers by value at `Double` (fixtures/builtin_cmp_eq_double_witness_test.vibe).
// Write `Double::max(a, b)`, or `if a > b { a } else b` at the concrete type.

import @vibe/builtin { ord_max }

fn main() -> Unit allows Console {
  println("\{ord_max(1.5, 2.5)}")
}
